<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<!--
  <summary>
  Lists screen (custom window 1151): named media lists that port into the
  queue.
  </summary>
  <remarks>
  Left column (list 50) is one row per list, right column (list 51) the
  items of whichever list is selected on the left. Both are static lists
  bound to Home window properties published by service.py:update_lists
  (Lists.N.* and LI.N.*), the same pattern as the Favourites screen: the
  window is skin-owned so Kodi never binds its own content into it.

  Selection follows focus. Each left row carries an idx property and the
  service reads Container(50).ListItem.Property(idx) every tick while this
  window is up, so moving the cursor fills the right column; clicking a row
  jumps into its items. Clicking an item asks the service for its action
  menu (play now, move up, move down, remove). The footer buttons act on the
  selected list through Skin.String(list_command): new, port, port_shuffle
  and port_time on the row itself, and rename, delete and autoremove (the
  Remove Watched switch) in the List Options drop down that button 9009
  opens, see LISTS-OPTIONS-MENU. On the one list tied to Radarr (Skin
  Settings, Radarr) the drop down also holds Remove from Radarr,
  list_command radarr_remove, which asks before anything is sent
  (service.py, RADARR-REMOVE).

  The action row sits on a 120px band at the foot of the screen, or at the
  top just under the header when Skin.HasSetting(lists_actions_top) is on
  (Lists and Favourites settings). Nothing is laid out twice: the band, its
  divider and the button grouplist slide up on a time="0" conditional
  animation, and both columns slide down 120px to make room. Navigation
  needs no second wiring because up and down out of either list already
  land on the grouplist, and the grouplist returns to the list, whichever
  side of the columns it is on.

  LISTS-QUICK (Skin.HasSetting(lists_quick_buttons), Lists and Favourites
  settings): the focused item row shows up, down and remove buttons at its
  right end. Right and left step along them, OK on one moves the row or,
  for remove, asks first. A list row is a single focusable thing in Kodi,
  so the buttons are drawn in the focused layout and the pick lives in
  Window(home).Property(Lists.Quick).

  Porting copies the list into Kodi's video and/or music queue and starts it
  playing. Shuffled means the order is randomised before queueing, so the
  queue itself holds the jumbled order and Kodi's own shuffle stays off.

  Port by Time queues a random pick instead of the whole list, enough of it
  to fill a length the user gives as HH:MM. The length is remembered per
  list in lists.json and shown on the button, and the pick overshoots
  rather than falls short: the item that crosses the target is kept.
  </remarks>
-->
<window id="1151" type="window">
	<defaultcontrol always="true">50</defaultcontrol>
	<!-- With no lists yet list 50 has nothing focusable, so land on the
	     footer where New List lives. -->
	<onload condition="String.IsEmpty(Window(home).Property(Lists.Count)) | String.IsEqual(Window(home).Property(Lists.Count),0)">SetFocus(9000)</onload>
	<onload>ClearProperty(Lists.Quick,home)</onload>
	<controls>

		<include content="WindowBackground"/>
		<include content="HeaderBar">
			<param name="title" value="     $LOCALIZE[31024]"/>
		</include>

		<!-- Logo -->
		<control type="image">
			<left>20</left>
			<top>5</top>
			<width>80</width>
			<height>80</height>
			<aspectratio>keep</aspectratio>
			<texture>logo.png</texture>
		</control>

		<!-- ===== Left column: the lists ===== -->
		<control type="label">
			<animation effect="slide" end="0,120" time="0" condition="Skin.HasSetting(lists_actions_top)">Conditional</animation>
			<left>60</left>
			<top>110</top>
			<width>560</width>
			<height>40</height>
			<font>font_small</font>
			<textcolor>text_dim</textcolor>
			<label>$LOCALIZE[31015]  $INFO[Window(home).Property(Lists.Count),(,)]</label>
		</control>

		<control type="list" id="50">
			<animation effect="slide" end="0,120" time="0" condition="Skin.HasSetting(lists_actions_top)">Conditional</animation>
			<left>60</left>
			<top>150</top>
			<width>560</width>
			<height>770</height>
			<onleft>50</onleft>
			<!-- LISTS-EMPTY-NAV: every line that hands focus to list 51
			     tests that it HOLDS something, not that it is visible. An
			     empty list is visible and cannot take focus; Kodi then
			     follows 51's own exit in the same direction, which for Up
			     and Down is the action row, so with an empty list selected
			     (every new list starts that way) focus could not leave the
			     row and the fallback lines were never reached. The property
			     test beside the count covers the moment when the column is
			     hidden and its list still holds the previous rows. -->
			<onright condition="Integer.IsGreater(Container(51).NumItems,0) + Integer.IsGreater(Window(home).Property(Lists.Sel.Count),0)">51</onright>
			<onright>9000</onright>
			<ondown>9000</ondown>
			<onup>9000</onup>
			<scrolltime tween="cubic" easing="out">200</scrolltime>
			<viewtype label="31014">list</viewtype>

			<itemlayout height="70" width="560">
				<control type="label">
					<left>20</left>
					<top>4</top>
					<width>520</width>
					<height>36</height>
					<font>font_reg</font>
					<textcolor>text</textcolor>
					<selectedcolor>$VAR[AccentHiColor]</selectedcolor>
					<aligny>center</aligny>
					<label>$INFO[ListItem.Label]</label>
				</control>
				<control type="label">
					<left>20</left>
					<top>38</top>
					<width>520</width>
					<height>28</height>
					<font>font_small</font>
					<textcolor>text_dim</textcolor>
					<selectedcolor>$VAR[AccentHiColor]</selectedcolor>
					<aligny>center</aligny>
					<label>$INFO[ListItem.Label2]</label>
				</control>
			</itemlayout>

			<focusedlayout height="70" width="560">
				<control type="image">
					<left>0</left>
					<top>0</top>
					<width>560</width>
					<height>70</height>
					<texture colordiffuse="$VAR[AccentColor]">white.png</texture>
					<visible>Control.HasFocus(50)</visible>
				</control>
				<control type="image">
					<left>0</left>
					<top>0</top>
					<width>560</width>
					<height>70</height>
					<texture colordiffuse="40FFFFFF">white.png</texture>
					<visible>!Control.HasFocus(50)</visible>
				</control>
				<control type="label">
					<left>20</left>
					<top>4</top>
					<width>520</width>
					<height>36</height>
					<font>font_reg</font>
					<textcolor>white</textcolor>
					<selectedcolor>white</selectedcolor>
					<aligny>center</aligny>
					<label>$INFO[ListItem.Label]</label>
				</control>
				<control type="label">
					<left>20</left>
					<top>38</top>
					<width>520</width>
					<height>28</height>
					<font>font_small</font>
					<textcolor>white</textcolor>
					<selectedcolor>white</selectedcolor>
					<aligny>center</aligny>
					<label>$INFO[ListItem.Label2]</label>
				</control>
			</focusedlayout>

			<content>
				<include content="ListsRows"/>
			</content>
		</control>

		<!-- ===== Right column: items of the selected list ===== -->
